    {
      "id": "49da6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "Cal State Apply Cal State LA Rongxiang Xu College of Health and Human Services Rongxiang Xu College of Health and Human Services Advising Center Degree with a Guarantee School of Social Work General Education Lower Division Courses University Catalog",
      "contentHtml": "<p><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/apply\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Cal&nbsp;State&nbsp;Apply</a></p><p><a href=\"http://www.calstatela.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Cal&nbsp;State&nbsp;LA</a></p><p><a href=\"http://www.calstatela.edu/hhs\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Rongxiang&nbsp;Xu&nbsp;College&nbsp;of&nbsp;Health&nbsp;and&nbsp;Human&nbsp;Services</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.calstatela.edu/hhs/ac\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Rongxiang&nbsp;Xu&nbsp;College&nbsp;of&nbsp;Health&nbsp;and&nbsp;Human&nbsp;Services&nbsp;Advising&nbsp;Center</a></p><p><a href=\"http://adegreewithaguarantee.com/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Degree&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;Guarantee</a></p><p><a href=\"https://www.calstatela.edu/hhs/sw\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">School&nbsp;of&nbsp;Social&nbsp;Work</a></p><p><a href=\"https://ecatalog.calstatela.edu/content.php?catoid=77&amp;navoid=11897\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">General&nbsp;Education&nbsp;Lower&nbsp;Division&nbsp;Courses</a></p><p><a href=\"http://ecatalog.calstatela.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">University&nbsp;Catalog</a></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "4fda6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 4,
      "content": "DIVERSITY REQUIREMENT FOR CAL STATE LA GRADUATION",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "afdd7145-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 5,
      "content": "The articulation information in Assist.org not only shows a link to the admission requirements (aka our Major Specific Criteria webpage) but also Cal State LA graduation requirements that may be completed at the lower-division level, prior to transferring to the University. The diversity requirement is a graduation requirement , not an admission requirement. The diversity requirement may be completed prior to, or after, transferring to the University. For the Cal State LA degree, students will be required to complete two courses (six units) certified as diversity courses, at least one focusing on issues of race and ethnicity and their intersectionality with other social categories that structure inequality in society. These courses can be completed either at the lower-division or upper-division level from among courses satisfying GE requirements. Please view the General Education agreements on Assist.org for the lower-division courses that will meet the Diversity (d) and Race &amp; Ethnicity (re) Requirements.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">The articulation information in Assist.org not only shows a link to the admission requirements (aka our </span><a href=\"http://www.calstatela.edu/admissions/major-specific-criteria\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Major Specific Criteria </a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">webpage) but also Cal State LA graduation requirements that may be completed at the lower-division level, prior to transferring to the University. The diversity requirement is a </span><strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(169, 62, 58);\">graduation requirement</strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">, not an admission requirement. The diversity requirement may be completed prior to, or after, transferring to the University. </span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">For the Cal State LA degree, students will be required to </span><strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(169, 62, 58);\">complete two courses (six units)</strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> certified as diversity courses, at least one focusing on issues of race and ethnicity and their intersectionality with other social categories that structure inequality in society. These courses can be completed either at the lower-division or upper-division level from among courses satisfying GE requirements.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Please view the </span><strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(169, 62, 58);\">General Education </strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">agreements on Assist.org for the lower-division courses that will meet the </span><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Diversity (d)</strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> and </span><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Race &amp; Ethnicity (re)</strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\"> Requirements.</span></p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "57da6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 6,
      "content": "Social Work, B.A.",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "55da6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 7,
      "content": "The Bachelor of Arts degree in Social Work enables students to explore and develop values, knowledge and generalist skills essential to the practice of social work in a multiethnic environment. The goals of the program include: providing continuing education for persons already employed in the field of social work or related human services; preparing students for professional entry-level positions in social work; and preparing students for further study in graduate schools of social work or related human services. The total number of units required for the Bachelor of Arts degree in Social Work (BASW) is 120, of which 57 or 58 units are in the major, including 6 or 7 units of required lower division courses, 45 units of required upper division courses, and 6 units of elective courses. Consult with an advisor for the specific number of units required in all areas of the degree including GE and free electives. See the Undergraduate Studies: General Information section for details about General Education and other requirements that constitute the units outside the major. School of Social Work Regulations Students in the Social Work major must earn grades of C or higher in the following social work courses: SW 3700, SW 3010, SW 3720, SW 4740, SW 4750, SW 4780, SW 3820, SW 4951 and SW 4952 . Students are required to complete a criminal clearance check, prior to entering a field placement. Some field agencies will not accept students who cannot pass the criminal background clearance. Please note that difficulty or the inability to place a student in a required field practicum may delay or prevent the completion of the Bachelor of Arts degree in Social Work degree.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">The&nbsp;Bachelor&nbsp;of&nbsp;Arts&nbsp;degree&nbsp;in&nbsp;Social&nbsp;Work&nbsp;enables&nbsp;students&nbsp;to&nbsp;explore&nbsp;and&nbsp;develop&nbsp;values,&nbsp;knowledge&nbsp;and&nbsp;generalist&nbsp;skills&nbsp;essential&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;practice&nbsp;of&nbsp;social&nbsp;work&nbsp;in&nbsp;a&nbsp;multiethnic&nbsp;environment.&nbsp;The&nbsp;goals&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;program&nbsp;include:&nbsp;providing&nbsp;continuing&nbsp;education&nbsp;for&nbsp;persons&nbsp;already&nbsp;employed&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;field&nbsp;of&nbsp;social&nbsp;work&nbsp;or&nbsp;related&nbsp;human&nbsp;services;&nbsp;preparing&nbsp;students&nbsp;for&nbsp;professional&nbsp;entry-level&nbsp;positions&nbsp;in&nbsp;social&nbsp;work;&nbsp;and&nbsp;preparing&nbsp;students&nbsp;for&nbsp;further&nbsp;study&nbsp;in&nbsp;graduate&nbsp;schools&nbsp;of&nbsp;social&nbsp;work&nbsp;or&nbsp;related&nbsp;human&nbsp;services.</span></p><p></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">The&nbsp;total&nbsp;number&nbsp;of&nbsp;units&nbsp;required&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;Bachelor&nbsp;of&nbsp;Arts&nbsp;degree&nbsp;in&nbsp;Social&nbsp;Work&nbsp;(BASW)&nbsp;is&nbsp;120,&nbsp;of&nbsp;which&nbsp;57&nbsp;or&nbsp;58&nbsp;units&nbsp;are&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;major,&nbsp;including&nbsp;6&nbsp;or&nbsp;7&nbsp;units&nbsp;of&nbsp;required&nbsp;lower&nbsp;division&nbsp;courses,&nbsp;45&nbsp;units&nbsp;of&nbsp;required&nbsp;upper&nbsp;division&nbsp;courses,&nbsp;and&nbsp;6&nbsp;units&nbsp;of&nbsp;elective&nbsp;courses.&nbsp;Consult&nbsp;with&nbsp;an&nbsp;advisor&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;specific&nbsp;number&nbsp;of&nbsp;units&nbsp;required&nbsp;in&nbsp;all&nbsp;areas&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;degree&nbsp;including&nbsp;GE&nbsp;and&nbsp;free&nbsp;electives.&nbsp;See&nbsp;the&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://ecatalog.calstatela.edu/content.php?catoid=77&amp;navoid=11897\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Undergraduate&nbsp;Studies:&nbsp;General&nbsp;Information</a><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;section&nbsp;for&nbsp;details&nbsp;about&nbsp;General&nbsp;Education&nbsp;and&nbsp;other&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;that&nbsp;constitute&nbsp;the&nbsp;units&nbsp;outside&nbsp;the&nbsp;major.</span></p><p><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">School&nbsp;of&nbsp;Social&nbsp;Work&nbsp;Regulations</strong></p><p></p><ul><li><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Students&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;Social&nbsp;Work&nbsp;major&nbsp;must&nbsp;earn&nbsp;grades&nbsp;of&nbsp;C&nbsp;or&nbsp;higher&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;following&nbsp;social&nbsp;work&nbsp;courses:&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">SW&nbsp;3700,&nbsp;SW&nbsp;3010,&nbsp;SW&nbsp;3720,&nbsp;SW&nbsp;4740,&nbsp;SW&nbsp;4750,&nbsp;SW&nbsp;4780,&nbsp;SW&nbsp;3820,&nbsp;SW&nbsp;4951</strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">&nbsp;and&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">SW&nbsp;4952</strong><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">.</span></li><li><span style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Students&nbsp;are&nbsp;required&nbsp;to&nbsp;complete&nbsp;a&nbsp;criminal&nbsp;clearance&nbsp;check,&nbsp;prior&nbsp;to&nbsp;entering&nbsp;a&nbsp;field&nbsp;placement.&nbsp;Some&nbsp;field&nbsp;agencies&nbsp;will&nbsp;not&nbsp;accept&nbsp;students&nbsp;who&nbsp;cannot&nbsp;pass&nbsp;the&nbsp;criminal&nbsp;background&nbsp;clearance.&nbsp;Please&nbsp;note&nbsp;that&nbsp;difficulty&nbsp;or&nbsp;the&nbsp;inability&nbsp;to&nbsp;place&nbsp;a&nbsp;student&nbsp;in&nbsp;a&nbsp;required&nbsp;field&nbsp;practicum&nbsp;may&nbsp;delay&nbsp;or&nbsp;prevent&nbsp;the&nbsp;completion&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;Bachelor&nbsp;of&nbsp;Arts&nbsp;degree&nbsp;in&nbsp;Social&nbsp;Work&nbsp;degree.</span></li></ul>"
    }
  ],
